#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0324-A expect=violation domain=PC
#note "The half this R-5.25 split sibling owns: row 4 has a numeric PCORRES above PCULOQ with PCSTRESC not 'ALQ' -> fires. Row 1 (below PCLLOQ without 'BLQ') is the PARENT CDISC-SEND-0324's state and must NOT fire here - the discriminator of the split, on the same dataset the parent's violation fixture uses."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=4 USUBJID=004
dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetic Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PCSEQ    type=Num
col PCTESTCD type=Char
col PCORRES  type=Char
col PCLLOQ   type=Num
col PCULOQ   type=Num
col PCSTRESC type=Char
---
S1 | PC | 001 | 1 | DRUGX | 2.5 | 5 | 100 | 2.5
S1 | PC | 002 | 1 | DRUGX | 3.1 | 5 | 100 | BLQ
S1 | PC | 003 | 1 | DRUGX | 50  | 5 | 100 | 50
S1 | PC | 004 | 1 | DRUGX | 250 | 5 | 100 | 250
S1 | PC | 005 | 1 | DRUGX | BLQ | 5 | 100 | BLQ
